      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Marlowe indexer is only pushing blocks to the DB which contain domain related transactions.\n\nWe need access to the current tip regardless of the content of the recent block to be able to assign reasonable tx validity value in our builder.\n\n* [ ] Add `ledger_attrs` table (details below) to our DB.\n* [ ] Change slightly the behavior of the Marlowe follower so it actually pushes new tip info to the persister.\n* [ ] Use this information on the persiter side and store the tip into the DB.\n\n```sql\nCREATE TYPE ledger_attr AS ENUM ('tip');\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ledger_state\n  ( value bytea\n  , attr ledger_attr PRIMARY KEY\n  );\n```",
      "closed_at": null,
      "closed_by": null,
